 **v6 additions (Tools, 2026-11-01).** `reel.mjs --hold 541,3301 [--hold-for 60] [--hold-every 6]` pauses on a tick (the sim is not stepped; the page keeps drawing) and takes a still every few seconds for a minute, with the mean change from still to still in `reel.json` `holds` (stills in `<out>/holds/`): ground that stays reads as a change near 0. `blackbox-clip.mjs --hold-at N` does the same on a tick of a recorded match. The page word `?splitshare=N` sets Camera's split share each frame (0.5 against the default 0.7). Parks added to the manifest: Camera's swing-share and lead-ahead (+ a fixup turning `lead_ahead` on), Encounter's beam-still, ground-settle, swing-warm, Simulation's field-place (+ Encounter's standing grant), Controls' first-pad, Audio's status line, Rendering's p to t (tile pool, coarse first, fill slice, tile level word, tundra strata) and Art's `data/art/biomes.json` overlay; the switches `splitShare` and `settle`.
 
-**The energy model on the page (Simulation's power-core, off by default).** `?power=1` puts `"power": true` in a match's setup (data/fight/power.json stays off); `?flatout=N` (3,500 to 7,000, the data's own range) or the slider shown with `?power=1` (bottom right, remembered in the browser, read at the start of the next match) sets `"flatOut"`, the base of flat-out flight. The parks `simulation-ceil-table` and `simulation-power-core` are in the manifest after field-place; CI has `Power check` and its negative control.
+**The energy model on the page (Simulation's power-core, on for the page).** Every match puts `"power": true` in its setup unless the address says `?power=0` or `?power=off` (then `"power": false`; the web drops a word valued 0, so the page reads its own address for it). While it's on, two sliders show bottom right (remembered in the browser as `orb_flatout` and `orb_travel`, read at the start of the next match): `"flatOut"`, the base of flat-out flight (3,500 to 7,000, or `?flatout=N`), and `"travel"`, how far a launch carries along the line (1.25 to 2.0 in steps of 0.05, default 2.0; `?travel=N` starts the slider there; Game Design's slam-and-pace.md section 2). The parks `simulation-ceil-table` and `simulation-power-core` are in the manifest after field-place; CI has `Power check` and its negative control.
 
